        '6-8', $q$A Later Start for Westbrook$q$, $q$(1) Many students at Westbrook Middle School arrive at first period yawning and struggling to focus. (2) Our school should move the start of the day from 7:30 to 8:30 in the morning. (3) Scientists who study sleep report that teenagers' bodies naturally fall asleep later at night than younger children's bodies do. (4) As a result, an early bell forces many students to wake up before they have rested enough. (5) In a survey our student council gave last spring, 68 percent of eighth graders said they feel tired during morning classes. (6) My cousin goes to a school in another state, and he likes his teachers a lot.

(7) Some parents argue that a later start would make after-school sports end too late. (8) This concern is reasonable, since practices already run until 5:00. (9) However, teams could use the gym lights and shorten warm-ups, and several nearby schools have adjusted their schedules this way without canceling any games. (10) A later start would also cut down on the number of students who are late for first period.

(11) Honestly, waking up early is the worst and everybody hates it. (12) For all these reasons, I think we should do something about the schedule.$q$, 'draft')
