        '6-8', $q$A Garden on Elm Street$q$, $q$(1) On the corner of Elm Street and Third Avenue sits an empty lot covered in weeds and broken glass. (2) Gardens are nice. (3) The city should turn this lot into a community garden that neighbors can share. (4) A garden would give families who live in apartments a place to grow fresh vegetables. (5) According to the county health department, residents in our neighborhood must travel more than a mile to reach a store that sells fresh produce. (6) A garden would also bring people together. (7) Neighbors who work side by side on weekends tend to get to know one another, and they look out for each other afterward.

(8) Some people claim that a garden would cost the city too much money. (9) A local hardware store has already offered to donate tools and lumber for raised beds, and volunteers from the high school have signed up to help build them. (10) The city's main expense would be a water connection, which the parks office estimates at about $2,000. (11) That's like nothing compared to what the city spends cleaning up the lot every year.

(12) A community garden would turn an eyesore into something the whole neighborhood can be proud of.$q$, 'draft')
