   $q$Which revision of sentence (9) best responds to the opposing claim with sound reasoning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The stations do cost a lot, so maybe the district should wait a few years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"abandons-claim"},{"text":"The stations are obviously worth it, since everyone knows plastic is bad.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"circular-reasoning"},{"text":"However, people who worry about money are not thinking about the future.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"attacks-opponent"},{"text":"However, each station can replace thousands of plastic bottles, so its cost is spread across years of use.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$However, each station can replace thousands of plastic bottles, so its cost is spread across years of use.$q$, $q$The correct revision answers the cost concern with a reason: the price is spread over long use. The choice about people not thinking about the future attacks opponents instead of answering their point.$q$, 'draft', '8f8fdcce-3cf8-5a35-9d02-cbb7d2a40f51')
