   $q$Read the sentence: "Kofi please pass the beakers to the next table." Which revision is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Kofi, please pass the beakers to the next table.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Kofi please pass the beakers, to the next table.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-before-prepositional-phrase"},{"text":"Kofi please, pass the beakers to the next table.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-after-please"},{"text":"Kofi please pass, the beakers to the next table.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-between-verb-object"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Kofi, please pass the beakers to the next table.$q$, $q$Kofi is being spoken to directly, so a comma sets off his name from the rest of the sentence. A comma after "please" leaves the name of the person addressed unmarked.$q$, 'draft', null)
