   $q$Which choice best uses punctuation to show that Omar pauses and hesitates while speaking?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"I was sure I packed the map, but... maybe not,\" Omar said slowly.","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"I was sure I packed the map, but; maybe not,\" Omar said slowly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-for-pause"},{"text":"\"I was sure I packed the map, but maybe, not,\" Omar said slowly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-misplaced"},{"text":"\"I was sure I packed the map but maybe not,\" Omar said slowly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"no-pause-marked"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"I was sure I packed the map, but... maybe not," Omar said slowly.$q$, $q$An ellipsis after "but" shows Omar's voice pausing as he starts to doubt himself. The semicolon is wrong because a semicolon joins two complete clauses and does not show a hesitation in speech.$q$, 'draft', null)
