   $q$Which sentence correctly punctuates the clause that adds extra, nonessential information?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The Amazon River, which flows through several countries, carries a huge amount of water.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The Amazon River which flows through several countries, carries a huge amount of water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-opening-comma"},{"text":"The Amazon River, which flows through several countries carries a huge amount of water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-closing-comma"},{"text":"The Amazon River which flows, through several countries carries a huge amount of water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splits-clause"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The Amazon River, which flows through several countries, carries a huge amount of water.$q$, $q$The clause "which flows through several countries" is extra information about a river already named, so commas go on both sides of it. Leaving out the closing comma runs the clause into the main verb "carries."$q$, 'draft', null)
