   $q$Which sentence uses commas correctly with the date and the place?$q$, $q$[{"text":"On March 3 2025, the robotics team traveled to Dayton Ohio, for a regional contest.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-internal-comma"},{"text":"On March 3, 2025, the robotics team traveled to Dayton, Ohio, for a regional contest.","is_correct":true},{"text":"On March 3, 2025 the robotics team traveled to Dayton, Ohio for a regional contest.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-closing-comma"},{"text":"On March, 3 2025, the robotics team traveled to Dayton, Ohio, for a regional contest.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-inside-date"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$On March 3, 2025, the robotics team traveled to Dayton, Ohio, for a regional contest.$q$, $q$A comma separates the day from the year and the city from the state, and another comma follows the year and the state when the sentence continues. The sentence with "2025 the robotics team" leaves out those closing commas after "2025" and "Ohio."$q$, 'draft', null)
