   $q$Read the sentence: "Yesterday aunt Rosa and my Uncle built a birdhouse for grandma." In the corrected sentence, which family words should be capitalized?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Aunt, Uncle, and Grandma","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"family-word-after-possessive-capitalized"},{"text":"Aunt only, but not uncle or grandma","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"name-use-lowercased"},{"text":"Aunt and Grandma, but not uncle","is_correct":true},{"text":"Uncle only, as it is now written","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"title-before-name-lowercased"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Aunt and Grandma, but not uncle$q$, $q$"Aunt" is part of the name "Aunt Rosa," and "Grandma" is used as her name, so both are capitalized, but "uncle" after "my" is a common noun. Capitalizing "Uncle" after "my" is the tempting mistake.$q$, 'draft', null)
