   $q$Read the sentence: "Her hands shaking with excitement Wen opened the envelope." Which revision is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Her hands shaking with excitement Wen, opened the envelope.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-between-subject-verb"},{"text":"Her hands shaking with excitement, Wen opened the envelope.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Her hands, shaking with excitement Wen opened the envelope.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splits-phrase"},{"text":"Her hands shaking, with excitement Wen opened the envelope.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splits-phrase"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Her hands shaking with excitement, Wen opened the envelope.$q$, $q$The opening phrase "Her hands shaking with excitement" ends before "Wen," so a comma goes there to mark the break. A comma after "Wen" splits the subject from the verb "opened."$q$, 'draft', null)
