   $q$In this sentence, the captain is speaking and the coach is the one who was late. Which version is punctuated to show that meaning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The coach, said the captain, was late.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The coach said, the captain was late.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-before-indirect-speech"},{"text":"The coach said the captain was late.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"meaning-reversed"},{"text":"The coach said the captain, was late.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-between-subject-verb"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The coach, said the captain, was late.$q$, $q$Commas around "said the captain" mark it as an interruption, so the main sentence becomes "The coach was late." Without those commas, the coach is the speaker and the captain is the one who was late.$q$, 'draft', null)
