   $q$Read the sentence: "Elena mixed the batter, and then the oven was preheated by her." Which revision fixes the shift in voice?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Elena mixed the batter, and then she preheated the oven.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Elena mixed the batter, and then the oven was preheated.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"voice-shift"},{"text":"Elena mixes the batter, and then the oven was preheated by her.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"tense-shift"},{"text":"The batter was mixed by Elena, and then she preheated the oven.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"voice-shift"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Elena mixed the batter, and then she preheated the oven.$q$, $q$Both clauses should use the active voice with Elena as the doer, as in "Elena mixed the batter, and then she preheated the oven." The choice "The batter was mixed by Elena" only reverses the problem, moving from passive to active.$q$, 'draft', null)
