   $q$Read the sentence: "First, read the directions carefully, and then you should label your diagram." Which revision fixes the shift in mood?$q$, $q$[{"text":"First, read the directions carefully, and then you will label your diagram.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mood-shift"},{"text":"First, read the directions carefully, and then label your diagram.","is_correct":true},{"text":"First, read the directions carefully, and then you label your diagram.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mood-shift"},{"text":"First, you should read the directions carefully, and then label your diagram.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mood-shift"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$First, read the directions carefully, and then label your diagram.$q$, $q$The sentence begins with a command, so both parts should stay in the imperative mood: "read" and "label." The choice starting "First, you should read" still shifts, this time from "you should read" to the command "label."$q$, 'draft', null)
