   $q$Read the sentence: "Running toward the bus stop, the rain soaked Kofi's backpack." Which revision fixes the dangling participle?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Running toward the bus stop, Kofi's backpack was soaked by the rain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dangling-participle"},{"text":"Running toward the bus stop, Kofi felt the rain soak his backpack.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Running toward the bus stop, the rain was soaking Kofi's backpack.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dangling-participle"},{"text":"The rain soaked Kofi's backpack, running toward the bus stop.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-participle"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Running toward the bus stop, Kofi felt the rain soak his backpack.$q$, $q$The participial phrase "Running toward the bus stop" must describe the person running, so "Kofi" has to follow it. In the choice "Running toward the bus stop, Kofi's backpack was soaked by the rain," the phrase still describes the backpack, which cannot run.$q$, 'draft', null)
