-- Passage wg8-informative-writing-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('4f42c6db-fd3c-530c-bf2d-15256314c9e2', 'wg8-informative-writing-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-informative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Libero$q$, $q$(1) Fans watching a volleyball match may notice one player wearing a jersey that does not match the rest of the team. (2) That player is the libero, a defensive specialist who plays only in the back row. (3) The word "libero" comes from Italian and means "free." (4) The name fits because the libero can move in and out of the game without using up the team's regular substitutions.

(5) The libero's main job is to receive serves and keep hard-driven attacks from hitting the floor. (6) A save made by diving or reaching low to pass a hard hit is called a dig. (7) A strong libero might record more than twenty digs in a single match. (8) Because the libero stays in the back row, the rules do not allow this player to attack the ball from above the height of the net.

(9) The libero also helps lead the defense. (10) She calls out where opponents are likely to hit and helps teammates shift into position. (11) The different jersey makes the libero easy for referees to track during fast substitutions. (12) Our school gym was painted blue last year.$q$, 'draft')
