-- Passage wg8-narrative-writing-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('4bde5af7-c78b-5cd5-874a-1185363bc282', 'wg8-narrative-writing-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-narrative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Bird Count$q$, $q$(1) At six in the morning, Grandpa Teodor and I stood at the edge of Hollow Creek Marsh with binoculars, a notebook, and a thermos of cocoa. (2) It was the day of the winter bird count, and our job was to record every bird we saw in our section. (3) I had never done it before. (4) Grandpa had done it for twenty-two years.

(5) For the first hour, I saw nothing but cattails and gray sky. (6) Grandpa, on the other hand, kept calling out names. (7) "Song sparrow. Two mallards. Red-winged blackbird." (8) I wrote them down, but secretly I wondered if he was making some of them up. (9) Grandpa thought I was bored and wished he had come alone.

(10) Then something moved in the reeds. (11) It was a tall brown bird standing perfectly still with its beak pointed at the sky. (12) I nudged Grandpa. (13) He lowered his binoculars slowly. (14) "A bittern," he whispered. (15) "In twenty-two years, I have seen one only twice."

(16) I wrote the name in the notebook.$q$, 'draft')
