   $q$Which revision of sentence 16 would best conclude the narrative by showing how the narrator has changed?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Grandpa had done the bird count for twenty-two years before that day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-earlier-detail"},{"text":"As I wrote the name in my neatest handwriting, I stopped doubting Grandpa and started searching the reeds myself.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The bird count is held every winter in many places around the country.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"},{"text":"Then I wrote down another song sparrow and two more mallards.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"anticlimax-no-reflection"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$As I wrote the name in my neatest handwriting, I stopped doubting Grandpa and started searching the reeds myself.$q$, $q$The correct choice connects to sentence 8, where the narrator doubted Grandpa, and shows that the doubt is gone. Repeating that Grandpa did the count for twenty-two years only restates sentence 4.$q$, 'draft', '4bde5af7-c78b-5cd5-874a-1185363bc282')
