   $q$Sentences 13 and 14 summarize a conversation. Which revision uses dialogue to reveal something new?$q$, $q$[{"text":"I told my mom all about the letters, and she told me she already knew.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"summary-not-dialogue"},{"text":"\"Did you know these were up here?\" I asked. Mom sat down beside me. \"Grandma used to read them to me.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"I am definitely going to get an A on this,\" I told her proudly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dialogue-off-focus"},{"text":"\"Letters,\" I said to her. \"Yes, letters,\" she said back to me.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dialogue-reveals-nothing"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Did you know these were up here?" I asked. Mom sat down beside me. "Grandma used to read them to me."$q$, $q$The correct choice uses real dialogue and reveals that the letters were shared across generations. The choice "I told my mom all about the letters, and she told me she already knew" still summarizes the talk instead of letting the characters speak.$q$, 'draft', 'b8b6da68-3cce-5c31-a362-e882a6d91854')
