   $q$Read the sentence: "In the event that the gym is unavailable, practice will be held in the cafeteria, which is the room that is located next to the library." Which revision is concise and keeps all of the information?$q$, $q$[{"text":"In the event the gym is unavailable, practice is held in the cafeteria room located next to the library.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-wordiness"},{"text":"If the gym is unavailable, practice will be in the cafeteria.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-key-meaning"},{"text":"If the gym is unavailable, practice will be in the cafeteria next to the library.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Practice will be held in the cafeteria next to the library.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-key-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$If the gym is unavailable, practice will be in the cafeteria next to the library.$q$, $q$"If" replaces "in the event that," and "next to the library" replaces a long clause, while every fact stays. The choice "If the gym is unavailable, practice will be in the cafeteria" is shorter still, but it drops where the cafeteria is.$q$, 'draft', null)
