   $q$A paragraph about the Lantern Comet begins, "The Lantern Comet returns every 76 years. Its tail glows a pale green." Which sentence best continues the paragraph while keeping the comet as the focus?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Esi Mensah, a student astronomer, was the first person to see it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"actor-focus-wrong-purpose"},{"text":"Spot the comet with a telescope in the early morning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-mood-for-purpose"},{"text":"A student astronomer named Esi Mensah first spotted it in 1931.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"actor-focus-wrong-purpose"},{"text":"The comet was first spotted in 1931 by a student astronomer.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The comet was first spotted in 1931 by a student astronomer.$q$, $q$The passive voice keeps "the comet" as the subject, just like the two sentences before it. The choice that begins "A student astronomer named Esi Mensah" is clear and active, but it shifts the subject to the astronomer and breaks the paragraph's focus.$q$, 'draft', null)
