   $q$A student is writing the last sentence of a speech urging classmates to help clean Willow Park. Which sentence uses the imperative mood to create the strongest call to action?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Willow Park will be cleaned on Saturday morning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"states-fact"},{"text":"We would love it if some of you could join us on Saturday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"softens-call-to-action"},{"text":"If you joined us, the park would look better.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"softens-call-to-action"},{"text":"Join us on Saturday and help bring Willow Park back to life.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Join us on Saturday and help bring Willow Park back to life.$q$, $q$"Join us" and "help" are imperative verbs that speak directly to the audience and ask for action. The conditional choices sound polite, but they soften the request instead of rallying listeners.$q$, 'draft', null)
