   $q$Read the sentence: "It seems like the data kind of suggest that maybe plants grow faster under blue light." Which revision is precise and appropriately cautious?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The data prove that all plants grow faster under blue light.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overclaims"},{"text":"Plants grow under blue light.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-key-meaning"},{"text":"It seems the data kind of suggest plants maybe grow faster in blue light.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-wordiness"},{"text":"The data suggest that plants may grow faster under blue light.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The data suggest that plants may grow faster under blue light.$q$, $q$"Suggest" and "may" keep one honest note of caution, while the extra hedges are cut. "The data prove that all plants" removes the hedging but claims far more than one test can show.$q$, 'draft', null)
