   $q$Read the sentence: "Dev wants either to join the robotics team or the debate club." Which revision places the correlative conjunctions correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Dev either wants to join the robotics team or the debate club.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"correlative-misplaced"},{"text":"Dev wants to join either the robotics team or the debate club.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Dev wants either to join the robotics team or debate club.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"correlative-misplaced"},{"text":"Dev wants either joining the robotics team or the debate club.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"verb-form-change"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Dev wants to join either the robotics team or the debate club.$q$, $q$"Either" and "or" should each come right before matching parts, here the two noun phrases "the robotics team" and "the debate club." In the original, "either" comes before a verb phrase but "or" comes before a noun phrase.$q$, 'draft', null)
