   $q$Read the sentence: "The festival was not only fun but also it raised money for the animal shelter." Which revision is parallel?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The festival was not only fun but also it was raising money for the animal shelter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"clause-after-correlative"},{"text":"The festival not only was fun but also raised money for the animal shelter.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The festival was not only fun, it also raised money for the animal shelter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"Not only the festival was fun but also raised money for the animal shelter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"correlative-misplaced"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The festival not only was fun but also raised money for the animal shelter.$q$, $q$"Not only" and "but also" are each followed by a verb phrase ("was fun" and "raised money"), so the two parts match. The comma version joins two independent clauses with only a comma, which is a comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
