   $q$Read the sentences: "Our class visited the Harbor Science Center. A museum with a giant tank of jellyfish." Which revision fixes the fragment?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Our class visited the Harbor Science Center, a museum with a giant tank of jellyfish.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Our class visited the Harbor Science Center; a museum with a giant tank of jellyfish.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-before-fragment"},{"text":"Our class visited the Harbor Science Center, it is a museum with a giant tank of jellyfish.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"Our class visited the Harbor Science Center. A museum, with a giant tank of jellyfish.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-does-not-fix-fragment"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Our class visited the Harbor Science Center, a museum with a giant tank of jellyfish.$q$, $q$"A museum with a giant tank of jellyfish" is an appositive that renames the science center, so it attaches with a comma. Adding "it is" makes a second independent clause, and joining it with only a comma creates a comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
