   $q$Read the sentence: "Hana's sister plays the cello she practices for an hour every night." Which revision fixes the error and keeps both ideas?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Hana's sister plays the cello she practices, for an hour every night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"run-on-unfixed"},{"text":"Hana's sister plays the cello. Practices for an hour every night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-created"},{"text":"Hana's sister plays the cello, she practices for an hour every night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"Hana's sister plays the cello, and she practices for an hour every night.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Hana's sister plays the cello, and she practices for an hour every night.$q$, $q$A comma plus "and" correctly joins the two independent clauses. Splitting the sentence after "cello" and dropping "she" leaves the second part without a subject, which is a fragment.$q$, 'draft', null)
