insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('43ab52c5-09ae-5dc4-899a-b9f6c7924340', 'wg8-writing-with-evidence-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Draft: The Robot and the Berries$q$, $q$(1) In "Robots in the Strawberry Field," Hollis Grant describes a farm that tested a picking robot for one season. (2) ____. (3) On the one hand, the robot could work through the night, and Grant reports that it picked "about the same number of berries as four workers." (4) It also never needed a break on hot afternoons. (5) On the other hand, the robot had trouble finding ripe berries hidden under leaves. (6) Grant writes that it "left nearly one berry in five on the plant." (7) My cousin has a robot vacuum that also gets stuck under furniture. (8) In the end, the farm owner, Rosa Delgado, kept her human pickers and used the robot only for night shifts.

(9) Delgado's choice shows that the article's real point is about balance. (10) The robot added speed, while people added the careful eye that the machine lacked.$q$, 'draft')
