   $q$Which sentence best fills blank 6 by explaining the evidence in sentence 5?$q$, $q$[{"text":"This shows that running every day is the only real way for a runner to improve.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-evidence"},{"text":"Forty seconds is quite a long time for anyone to wait during a race.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-explanation"},{"text":"Since the rested group improved more than three times as much, the study supports Mensah's point that rest builds speed.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The study that Mensah describes lasted for a total of eight weeks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Since the rested group improved more than three times as much, the study supports Mensah's point that rest builds speed.$q$, $q$Forty seconds compared with twelve is more than three times the improvement, and the choice beginning "Since the rested group improved" ties that comparison to the claim. Saying that daily running is the only way to improve contradicts the results in sentence 5.$q$, 'draft', '8ca33250-10a4-57a2-af28-2f3bad0a991c')
