-- Passage wg8-writing-with-evidence-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('a9580e23-ac5e-5950-87da-7296db5e38be', 'wg8-writing-with-evidence-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Draft: Lunch Without Phones$q$, $q$(1) In "The Quiet Phone Experiment," Ruth Abara reports on a school that asked students to leave their phones in lockers during lunch for one month. (2) Abara shows that the rule led students to talk with each other more, even though many disliked it at first. (3) At the start, Abara writes, "a petition against the rule gathered more than two hundred names." (4) By the third week, however, lunch monitors noticed more students playing board games and chatting across tables. (5) ____, the cafeteria had become noticeably louder. (6) Phones have changed a great deal since they were first invented. (7) In a survey at the end of the month, sixty percent of students said they had made a new friend at lunch.

(8) Abara also includes the view of eighth grader Tobias Lindqvist. (9) He told her that he missed checking game scores during lunch but liked "actually knowing the kids at my table." (10) Tobias's mixed feelings match the article as a whole.

(11) That is why phones should be banned everywhere.$q$, 'draft')
