   $q$Read the sentence: "Her backpack slung over one shoulder, my sister jogged toward the library." What kind of phrase is "Her backpack slung over one shoulder"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"a participial phrase","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-absolute-participial"},{"text":"a prepositional phrase","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-absolute-prepositional"},{"text":"an independent clause","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"phrase-called-clause"},{"text":"an absolute phrase","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$an absolute phrase$q$, $q$The phrase has its own noun ("backpack") followed by a participle ("slung") and modifies the whole sentence, which makes it an absolute phrase. A participial phrase would start with the participle and describe a noun directly, without its own subject.$q$, 'draft', null)
