   $q$Read the sentences: "The storm finally ended. The ferry left the dock." Which choice combines them using an absolute phrase?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The storm having finally ended, the ferry left the dock.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Because the storm finally ended, the ferry left the dock.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"uses-clause-instead"},{"text":"The storm finally ended, the ferry left the dock.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice"},{"text":"Having finally ended, the ferry left the dock.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dangling-modifier"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The storm having finally ended, the ferry left the dock.$q$, $q$"The storm having finally ended" has its own noun plus a participle and modifies the whole sentence, so it is an absolute phrase. "Because the storm finally ended" is correct grammar, but it is an adverbial clause, not an absolute phrase.$q$, 'draft', null)
