   $q$Read the sentence: "Restoring old radios takes patience and steady hands." What is "Restoring old radios"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"an absolute phrase modifying the sentence","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-gerund-absolute"},{"text":"a gerund phrase acting as the subject","is_correct":true},{"text":"a participial phrase describing a noun","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-gerund-participial"},{"text":"an adverbial clause telling how","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"phrase-called-clause"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$a gerund phrase acting as the subject$q$, $q$"Restoring old radios" names an activity and is the subject of "takes," so it is a gerund phrase working as a noun. It looks like a participial phrase, but it does not describe any noun.$q$, 'draft', null)
