   $q$Read the sentence: "The students who had finished their lab reports left early." Because the relative clause has no commas, what does the sentence mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Every student had finished a report, and all of them left early.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-restrictive-nonrestrictive"},{"text":"The students left early so that they could finish their reports.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-clause-function"},{"text":"Only the students who had finished their reports left early.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The reports were finished because the students left early.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Only the students who had finished their reports left early.$q$, $q$Without commas, the clause "who had finished their lab reports" limits which students are meant, so only those students left early. With commas, it would describe all of the students, which is the tempting but wrong reading.$q$, 'draft', null)
